# Hand-written entries for the core dictionaries, for keywords where the
# OpenFOAM tree states a type but no meaning. Appended by makeDictatorHelp.
# A "SubDict.key" path records a standard key of a named sub-dictionary, which
# "dictator <file> SubDict -help" tables; see the PIMPLE/SIMPLE/PISO block below.
# scope	path	type	required	default	options	description	source
controlDict	application	word	optional			Name of the solver executable run for this case.	curated
controlDict	startFrom	word	optional	latestTime	firstTime;startTime;latestTime	Which time directory the run starts from.	curated
controlDict	startTime	scalar	required with startFrom startTime			Time to start from, used when startFrom is startTime.	curated
controlDict	stopAt	word	optional	endTime	endTime;writeNow;noWriteNow;nextWrite	Condition under which the run stops.	curated
controlDict	endTime	scalar	required with stopAt endTime			Time at which the run stops, used when stopAt is endTime.	curated
controlDict	deltaT	scalar	required			Time step. The initial time step when adjustTimeStep is on.	curated
controlDict	writeControl	word	optional	timeStep	timeStep;runTime;adjustable;adjustableRunTime;clockTime;cpuTime;none	What writeInterval is counted in. adjustable also nudges the time step so writes land on exact intervals.	curated
controlDict	writeInterval	scalar	required			Interval between writes, in the unit chosen by writeControl.	curated
controlDict	purgeWrite	label	optional	0		Number of time directories to keep, oldest deleted first. 0 keeps all.	curated
controlDict	writeFormat	word	optional	ascii	ascii;binary	Format of the written field files.	curated
controlDict	writePrecision	label	optional	6		Significant figures used when writing ascii fields.	curated
controlDict	writeCompression	Switch	optional	off		Whether written files are gzip compressed.	curated
controlDict	timeFormat	word	optional	general	general;fixed;scientific	Format of the time directory names.	curated
controlDict	timePrecision	label	optional	6		Significant figures in the time directory names.	curated
controlDict	runTimeModifiable	Switch	optional	false		Whether dictionaries are re-read at the start of each time step, so a case can be changed while it runs. Off by default, though most tutorials switch it on.	curated
controlDict	adjustTimeStep	Switch	optional	false		Whether the time step is adjusted to satisfy the Courant limits.	curated
controlDict	maxCo	scalar	optional	1		Maximum Courant number allowed when adjustTimeStep is on.	curated
controlDict	maxAlphaCo	scalar	required			Maximum Courant number evaluated at the interface, read by the VoF solvers alongside maxCo. Usually the binding limit for interface capturing. Has no default: a VoF solver that computes an interface Courant number stops without it.	curated
controlDict	maxDeltaT	scalar	optional	GREAT		Upper limit on the time step when adjustTimeStep is on. The default GREAT means no limit, so the Courant condition alone sets the step.	curated
controlDict	graphFormat	word	optional	raw		Format of graph data written by function objects.	curated
controlDict	libs	wordList	optional			Extra libraries loaded at start-up, for solvers, models or function objects not in the executable.	curated
controlDict	functions	dictionary	optional			Function objects run during the simulation, for sampling, monitoring and derived fields.	curated
fvSolution	solvers	dictionary	required			Linear solver settings, one sub-dictionary per field.	curated
fvSolution	solver	word	required		PCG;PBiCG;PBiCGStab;GAMG;smoothSolver;diagonal;PPCG;PPCR	Linear solver used for this field. PCG and GAMG suit symmetric matrices such as pressure, PBiCGStab the asymmetric ones.	curated
fvSolution	preconditioner	word	required by PCG, PBiCG and PBiCGStab		DIC;DILU;diagonal;FDIC;GAMG;none	Preconditioner for a Krylov solver. DIC pairs with symmetric matrices, DILU with asymmetric.	curated
fvSolution	smoother	word	required by GAMG and smoothSolver		GaussSeidel;symGaussSeidel;DIC;DICGaussSeidel;DILU;DILUGaussSeidel	Smoother used by GAMG and smoothSolver.	curated
fvSolution	tolerance	scalar	optional	1e-6		Absolute residual at which the linear solve stops.	curated
fvSolution	relTol	scalar	optional	0		Factor by which the residual must fall within one solve. 0, the default, forces the solve to the absolute tolerance, which is what a final corrector normally wants.	curated
fvSolution	maxIter	label	optional	1000		Maximum iterations of the linear solver.	curated
fvSolution	nSweeps	label	optional	1		Sweeps performed by the smoother between residual checks.	curated
fvSolution	nCellsInCoarsestLevel	label	optional	10		Cells in the coarsest GAMG level, where the equation is solved directly.	curated
fvSolution	agglomerator	word	optional	faceAreaPair	faceAreaPair;algebraicPair	How GAMG groups cells when coarsening.	curated
fvSolution	mergeLevels	label	optional	1		GAMG levels merged per coarsening step.	curated
fvSolution	cacheAgglomeration	Switch	optional	true		Whether the GAMG agglomeration is kept between solves. Turn off on a moving mesh.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE	dictionary	optional			Controls for the PIMPLE pressure-velocity loop used by transient solvers.	curated
fvSolution	SIMPLE	dictionary	optional			Controls for the SIMPLE pressure-velocity loop used by steady solvers.	curated
fvSolution	PISO	dictionary	optional			Controls for the PISO pressure-velocity loop.	curated
fvSolution	nCorrectors	label	optional	1		Pressure corrector solves per outer iteration.	curated
fvSolution	nOuterCorrectors	label	optional	1		Outer iterations per time step. 1 makes PIMPLE behave as PISO; more allows a larger time step at the cost of work per step.	curated
fvSolution	nNonOrthogonalCorrectors	label	optional	0		Extra pressure solves correcting for mesh non-orthogonality.	curated
fvSolution	momentumPredictor	Switch	optional	true		Whether the momentum equation is solved before the pressure correction. Often off for interface-dominated flows.	curated
fvSolution	consistent	Switch	optional	false		Use SIMPLEC rather than SIMPLE, which tolerates larger relaxation factors.	curated
fvSolution	pRefCell	label	required when no boundary fixes the pressure			Cell whose pressure is pinned when no boundary sets the pressure level. The keyword follows the field name, so a VoF solver wants p_rghRefCell. Supply this or pRefPoint.	curated
fvSolution	pRefValue	scalar	required when no boundary fixes the pressure			Pressure imposed at pRefCell or pRefPoint. The keyword follows the field name, so a VoF solver wants p_rghRefValue.	curated
fvSolution	residualControl	dictionary	optional			Residual levels at which the outer loop or the run is considered converged.	curated
fvSolution	relaxationFactors	dictionary	optional			Under-relaxation applied to equations and fields.	curated
fvSolution	nAlphaCorr	label	required			Correctors applied to the phase fraction equation. Read from the alpha solver sub-dictionary, and has no default.	curated
fvSolution	nAlphaSubCycles	label	required			Sub-cycles of the phase fraction equation per time step, letting alpha run at a smaller step than the momentum equation. Read from the alpha solver sub-dictionary, and has no default.	curated
fvSolution	cAlpha	scalar	required by interFoam			Strength of the artificial interface compression used by MULES, read from the alpha solver sub-dictionary. Not used by isoAdvector, which resolves the interface geometrically, so interIsoFoam does not need it.	curated
fvSolution	MULESCorr	Switch	optional	false		Use the semi-implicit MULES limiter, which permits a larger alpha Courant number.	curated
fvSolution	nLimiterIter	label	optional	3		Iterations of the MULES limiter.	curated
fvSolution	alphaApplyPrevCorr	Switch	optional	false		Reuse the previous time step's MULES correction as a starting point.	curated
fvSolution	reconstructionScheme	word	required		isoAlpha;plicRDF;gradAlpha	How isoAdvector reconstructs the interface plane in each cell. plicRDF iterates on the reconstructed distance function and is more accurate on unstructured meshes. There is no default: the reconstruction reports a fatal error if the entry is absent.	curated
fvSolution	isoFaceTol	scalar	optional	1e-8		Tolerance for locating the isosurface within a cell.	curated
fvSolution	surfCellTol	scalar	optional	1e-8		Phase fraction bounds within which a cell counts as an interface cell.	curated
fvSolution	nAlphaBounds	label	optional	3		Passes of the bounding step applied to alpha after advection.	curated
fvSolution	snapTol	scalar	optional	0		Below this distance from 0 or 1, a phase fraction is snapped to it.	curated
fvSolution	clip	Switch	optional	true		Whether the phase fraction is clipped to [0,1].	curated
fvSchemes	ddtSchemes	dictionary	required			Discretisation of the time derivative.	curated
fvSchemes	gradSchemes	dictionary	required			Discretisation of gradient terms.	curated
fvSchemes	divSchemes	dictionary	required			Discretisation of divergence, that is convection, terms.	curated
fvSchemes	laplacianSchemes	dictionary	required			Discretisation of Laplacian, that is diffusion, terms.	curated
fvSchemes	interpolationSchemes	dictionary	required			Interpolation of cell values to faces.	curated
fvSchemes	snGradSchemes	dictionary	required			Discretisation of the surface-normal gradient.	curated
fvSchemes	fluxRequired	dictionary	optional			Fields for which the face flux is stored after the solve.	curated
fvSchemes	ddtSchemes.default	word	required		Euler;backward;CrankNicolson;steadyState;localEuler	Time scheme. Euler is first order and stable, backward and CrankNicolson second order and less dissipative, steadyState drops the term.	curated
fvSchemes	gradSchemes.default	word	required		Gauss linear;leastSquares;cellLimited Gauss linear 1	Gradient scheme. A cellLimited variant bounds the gradient on poor meshes.	curated
fvSchemes	divSchemes.default	word	required		none;Gauss linear;Gauss upwind;Gauss limitedLinear 1	Fallback convection scheme. Usually none, so that every divergence term must be named explicitly.	curated
fvSchemes	laplacianSchemes.default	word	required		Gauss linear corrected;Gauss linear limited corrected 0.33;Gauss linear orthogonal	Laplacian scheme. The trailing word sets the non-orthogonal correction; corrected suits a good mesh, limited a poor one.	curated
fvSchemes	interpolationSchemes.default	word	required		linear;cubic;midPoint	Cell-to-face interpolation.	curated
fvSchemes	snGradSchemes.default	word	required		corrected;limited corrected 0.33;orthogonal;uncorrected	Surface-normal gradient, with the same non-orthogonality trade-off as the Laplacian schemes.	curated
# standard keys of the pressure-velocity control sub-dictionaries, as
# "SubDict.key" records; dictator tables these under e.g. "fvSolution PIMPLE -help"
fvSolution	PIMPLE.nOuterCorrectors	label	optional	1		Outer PIMPLE iterations per time step. 1 makes PIMPLE behave as PISO; more lets you take a larger time step at the cost of work per outer iteration.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.nCorrectors	label	optional	1		Pressure-correction (PISO) solves per outer iteration.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.nNonOrthogonalCorrectors	label	optional	0		Extra pressure solves per corrector that correct for mesh non-orthogonality.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.momentumPredictor	Switch	optional	true		Whether the momentum equation is solved before the first pressure correction. Often turned off for interface-dominated or creeping flows.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.consistent	Switch	optional	false		Use the SIMPLEC-consistent formulation, which tolerates relaxation factors close to 1.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.transonic	Switch	optional	false		Use the transonic form of the pressure equation, for the compressible solvers that support it.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.turbOnFinalIterOnly	Switch	optional	true		Solve the turbulence equations only on the final outer iteration.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.finalOnLastPimpleIterOnly	Switch	optional	false		Apply the "final" relaxation factors and linear-solver settings only on the last outer iteration rather than as soon as the residual controls are met.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.ddtCorr	Switch	optional	true		Include the face-flux time-derivative correction in the pressure equation.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.solveFlow	Switch	optional	true		Solve the flow. Set false to advance only the other equations on a frozen velocity and flux field.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.SIMPLErho	Switch	optional	false		Update the density with the SIMPLE rather than the PIMPLE rule in compressible runs.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.frozenFlow	Switch	optional	false		Skip the flow solution entirely, advancing only the remaining equations.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.residualControl	dictionary	optional			Per-field convergence targets for the outer loop, as "field { tolerance <abs>; relTol <rel>; }". When every named field is within tolerance the outer loop ends early.	curated
fvSolution	SIMPLE.nNonOrthogonalCorrectors	label	optional	0		Extra pressure solves per step that correct for mesh non-orthogonality.	curated
fvSolution	SIMPLE.momentumPredictor	Switch	optional	true		Whether the momentum equation is solved before the pressure correction.	curated
fvSolution	SIMPLE.consistent	Switch	optional	false		Use SIMPLEC rather than SIMPLE. SIMPLEC tolerates relaxation factors close to 1 and usually needs fewer iterations.	curated
fvSolution	SIMPLE.transonic	Switch	optional	false		Use the transonic form of the pressure equation, for the compressible steady solvers that support it.	curated
fvSolution	SIMPLE.frozenFlow	Switch	optional	false		Skip the flow solution, advancing only other equations such as turbulence or energy.	curated
fvSolution	SIMPLE.residualControl	dictionary	optional			Initial-residual levels at which the steady run is converged and stops, one scalar per field, as "p 1e-3; U 1e-4;".	curated
fvSolution	PISO.nCorrectors	label	optional	1		Pressure-correction solves per time step.	curated
fvSolution	PISO.nNonOrthogonalCorrectors	label	optional	0		Extra pressure solves per corrector that correct for mesh non-orthogonality.	curated
fvSolution	PISO.momentumPredictor	Switch	optional	true		Whether the momentum equation is solved before the first pressure correction.	curated
fvSolution	PISO.transonic	Switch	optional	false		Use the transonic form of the pressure equation, for the compressible solvers that support it.	curated
fvSolution	PISO.consistent	Switch	optional	false		Consistent (SIMPLEC-style) formulation. Rarely used with PISO.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.pRefCell	label	optional			Cell whose pressure is pinned when no boundary sets the pressure level. The keyword follows the field name, so a VoF solver wants p_rghRefCell. Supply this or pRefPoint.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.pRefValue	scalar	optional			Pressure imposed at pRefCell or pRefPoint. The keyword follows the field name, so a VoF solver wants p_rghRefValue.	curated
fvSolution	PIMPLE.pRefPoint	vector	optional			Point whose nearest cell has its pressure pinned, field-name prefixed like pRefCell. An alternative to pRefCell.	curated
fvSolution	SIMPLE.pRefCell	label	optional			Cell whose pressure is pinned when no boundary sets the pressure level. The keyword follows the field name. Supply this or pRefPoint.	curated
fvSolution	SIMPLE.pRefValue	scalar	optional			Pressure imposed at pRefCell or pRefPoint. The keyword follows the field name.	curated
fvSolution	SIMPLE.pRefPoint	vector	optional			Point whose nearest cell has its pressure pinned, field-name prefixed like pRefCell. An alternative to pRefCell.	curated
fvSolution	PISO.pRefCell	label	optional			Cell whose pressure is pinned when no boundary sets the pressure level. The keyword follows the field name. Supply this or pRefPoint.	curated
fvSolution	PISO.pRefValue	scalar	optional			Pressure imposed at pRefCell or pRefPoint. The keyword follows the field name.	curated
fvSolution	PISO.pRefPoint	vector	optional			Point whose nearest cell has its pressure pinned, field-name prefixed like pRefCell. An alternative to pRefCell.	curated
